From: Kshitiz Godara <kgodara@microsoft.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Supply a hostname in the closed-socket SSLTransport test

The default SSL context enables hostname checking. Python 3.12.15 warns
when wrap_bio() is called without server_hostname, and the test suite
treats warnings as errors. Supply a hostname so the test reaches the
closed-socket OSError it is intended to verify.

diff --git a/test/test_ssltransport.py b/test/test_ssltransport.py
--- a/test/test_ssltransport.py
+++ b/test/test_ssltransport.py
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ class SingleTLSLayerTestCase(SocketDummyServerTestCase):
         context = ssl.create_default_context()
         sock.close()
         with pytest.raises(OSError):
-            SSLTransport(sock, context)
+            SSLTransport(sock, context, server_hostname="localhost")
 
     @pytest.mark.timeout(PER_TEST_TIMEOUT)
     def test_close_after_handshake(self) -> None:
